docs/*-risk-analysis.md
docs/pre-*-crypto-security-review.md
docs/manual-testing.md
scripts/nuclear-teardown.sh
scripts/golden-path-founder-cold.sh

# Execution docs: keep planning/, reference/, blocks/, current-state, README, startup prompt.
# Ignore only stale subtrees and one-off session artifacts under docs/execution/.
docs/execution/archive/
docs/execution/resume-prompts/
docs/execution/session-resume-prompt-*.md
docs/execution/testing-results.md
docs/execution/prompts/b*-restart-prompt.md
docs/execution/prompts/b*-start-prompt.md

# Ephemeral local workspaces
.worktrees/
b16-test-workspace/

# docs/execution/ is local-only build history and cloud planning (D90, 2026-07-28).
# Previously tracked files were removed from the index in the untrack commit;
# never re-add them. Public roadmap/known-limitations stay tracked.
docs/execution/

# ── PUBLIC-REPO GUARDRAIL (added 2026-08-08) ──────────────────────────────
# This is the PUBLIC open-source CLI repo. It contains code + user-facing
# product docs ONLY. Internal decision registers, PRDs, roadmaps, execution
# plans, block/OWA work records, founder/session artifacts, and PII must
# never be committed. The patterns above enforce path-based exclusion.
# Content-based exclusion (decision IDs, internal block vocabulary, personal
# identifiers, credential labels) is enforced by the guardrail CI workflow
# (.github/workflows/guardrail.yml). If you are tempted to commit a file and
# are unsure whether it is public-safe, it is not — keep it local or in the
# private cloud repo.
